[sliver] Unavoidable fitted lead-in: each strip is an eased edge of the cap's bore at its shoulder, 0.45 mm wide and running 10° round the bore, which guides a tube lying slightly off the rib's seat into the bore as the cap goes on.
alternatives: A wider ease wraps less of the tube in the cap's half of the pipe; none leaves a sharp bore edge to pinch the tube.
